From: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Subject: [PATCH 0/2] media: i2c: ak7375: add support for AK7374

The AK7374 is a voice coil motor camera lens actuator from the same
family as the AK7375 already supported by this driver. It is
register-compatible but uses 10-bit position values (shifted left by 6
in the 16-bit position register) with a 1024-step focus range, so it
slots in as a new chip definition plus a compatible string.

It is the main-camera (S5KGW1P, 64MP) focus actuator on the Samsung
Galaxy A52 (a52q, SM7125). Register values are taken from the vendor
CamX actuator driver and verified against the hardware.

Tested on the Galaxy A52 with kernel 6.14 (libcamera simple pipeline,
camss); not yet retested on 7.3.

